name: sim.writeCustomDataBlock
description: Deprecated. See sim.writeCustomStringData and sim.writeCustomBufferData instead
luaSynopsis: sim.writeCustomDataBlock(int objectHandle, string tagName, string/bytes data)
pythonSynopsis: sim.writeCustomDataBlock(int objectHandle, string tagName, buffer data)
inputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the object where you want to store your data, or sim.handle_scene if you wish to store the data with the scene, or sim.handle_app if you wish to store the data with the application's current session
2. tagName: string that identifies the data. An empty string removes all custom data blocks
3. data: your custom data. If empty, the current data under the specified dataName is removed
outputs:
replacedBy:
- name: setBufferProperty, class: object, object_setBufferProperty.method, note: "use a 'customData.'-prefix for the property name"
